          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*3. In a circle, if the distance of chord AB from the centre is twice the distance of another chord CD from the centre, then can we conclude that CD = 2 AB? Give reasons for your answer."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.187,
            0.575,
            0.211
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5.7 Angles Subtended by an Arc"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.221,
            0.886,
            0.283
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "An "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "arc",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of a circle is a connected portion of the circle. It is defined by two points on the circle, called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "end points",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of the arc, and the curve connecting them along the circle’s edge."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.137,
            0.301,
            0.438,
            0.51
          ],
          "content": [
